  "widgets": ["TextWidget", "SelectWidget", "CheckboxWidget", "TextAreaWidget"],
  "description": "Application for Federal Domestic Assistance - Short Organizational (SF424_Short_3_0) is a simplified SF-424 variant for organizational applicants. It collects the applicant organization, project information, a project director, an optional primary contact/grants administrator, and an authorized representative certification. It is shorter than the full SF-424: it omits funding estimates, state review, delinquent debt, and federal identifiers.",
  "sgg_form_id": "sf424_short",
  "notes": [
    "State requirement: DAT marks State as required (*) for both applicant and project director addresses. The XSD makes State optional within `AddressDataTypeV3` (in a choice group with Province, both minOccurs=\"0\"). Resolution: follow the XSD. State is conditionally required when Country is USA.",
    "ZIP/Postal Code requirement: DAT marks ZIP as required (*) for both applicant and project director addresses. The XSD marks `ZipPostalCode` as optional (minOccurs=\"0\"). Resolution: follow the XSD. ZIP is optional.",
    "Title requirement (Project Director): DAT marks Title as required (*) for the Project Director. The XSD makes `Title` optional within `ContactPersonDataTypeV3` (minOccurs=\"0\"). Resolution: follow the XSD for XML validation; the SGG implementation may enforce Title as required at the UI level.",
    "ZIP/Postal Code maxLength: The XSD defines `ZipPostalCodeDataType` with maxLength 30. We will use the XSD constraint (30) for validation.",
    "Province maxLength: The XSD defines `ProvinceDataType` with maxLength 30. We will use the XSD constraint (30).",
    "SAMUEIDataType: The XSD defines exact `length` of 12 (not maxLength 13). We will enforce exactly 12 characters.",
    "Other Applicant Type minLength: The XSD uses minLength 0 (not 1) for `ApplicantTypeOtherSpecify`, unlike most other string fields. This means an empty string is valid per the XSD."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "The \"Same as Project Director\" checkbox controls whether the Primary Contact section is populated. When checked, the `ContactPersonGroup` element should be omitted from XML (per minOccurs=\"0\"), or the SGG implementation should copy the data server-side.",
    "The AOR Name uses `HumanNameDataType` directly (not wrapped in a `ContactPersonDataTypeV3`), so the AOR does not have a separate address. The AOR Title, Phone, Fax, and Email are separate top-level elements, not nested.",
    "The form does not include funding estimates, state executive order review, or delinquent federal debt questions, making it simpler than the full SF-424.",
    "Web Address (`xs:anyURI`) has no maxLength in the XSD. Validation should accept any well-formed URI."
  ],
